    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d709-a2">

                <pb facs="1135" n="999" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg999"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The consul-general of Hayti to the consul of Santo
                        Domingo.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of Hayti at New York</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">New York</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-11-02"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 2, 1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Consul and Dear Colleague</hi>: Confirming the
                    conversation I have had with you upon the situation in Hayti, and in view of the
                    alliance existing between the two Republics which we have the honor to represent
                    in this city, I have inform you that it has come to our knowledge that agents of
                    the Haytian rebellion now in the United States are about to ship arms and
                    munitions of war to Dominican ports under the pretext that they are intended for
                    your Government.</p>
                <p>We have reason to believe that these articles, after having been landed in some
                    point in Santo Domingo, are to be sent to the territory or coast of Hayti, in
                    violation of Dominican neutrality. In warning you of these facts, I count upon
                    your benevolent co-operation, to the end that the good harmony between our
                    countries may not he imperilled by adventurers, at the same time leaving to whom
                    it may concern all official responsibilities.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. D. Bassett.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
